  "prefLabel": "Sw 701.01 Definitions",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-06-29",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Sw 701.01 Definitions. The following definitions shall apply:\n\n(a) “Sales rep” means an individual in the employ of the New Hampshire lottery commission working as a lottery sales representative as that job is described by the State of New Hampshire division of personnel in the department of administrative services;\n\n(b) “Incentive” means an amount of compensation over and above a sales representative’s salary, which is awarded based upon sales performance as set forth herein;\n\n(c) “Sales” means as settled instant game tickets less returns and adjustments; and\n\n(d) “Sales goal” means an amount of sales established at the first regular New Hampshire lottery commission meeting after the start of the fiscal year.\n\nSource. #10035, INTERIM, eff 1-1-12, EXPIRES: 6-29-12; ss by #10132, eff 5-23-12",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sw700.html"
